# Binary/IQ capture data — large, not tracked. Three lessons encoded here:
# the trailing slash matches directories only, so a symlink named `artifacts`
# slipped past it into a commit and a later checkout replaced the real
# directory with it, taking the ignored contents with it; the bare form
# catches the symlink; and BOTH are anchored with a leading slash, because an
# unanchored pattern matches at ANY depth — bare `artifacts` silently ignored
# tests/artifacts/, leaving 31 MB of irreplaceable off-air ground truth
# untracked on exactly one machine while its e2e gates skipped green in CI.
/artifacts/
/artifacts
# Superpowers working scaffolding (ephemeral plans/notes; lasting facts live in docs/)
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/superpowers
# Default MCP workspace when MARCONI_WORKSPACE is unset. Deliberately
# UNANCHORED, unlike /artifacts: run output is generated junk that appears
# wherever a server or test happened to run, never precious data — the
# anchoring lesson protects irreplaceable trees, not disposable ones.
marconi-runs/
marconi-runs
